cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use dienr, please cite it as below, and also cite the DENR paper, whose
  method dienr reimplements.
title: "dienr: Deconvolution of Isoform Expression from Nascent RNAs"
abstract: >-
  A Python reimplementation of DENR that explains nascent RNA sequencing signal
  (PRO-seq, GRO-seq) at each locus as a nonnegative mixture of pre-RNA isoform
  models, with reusable designs, explicit identifiability, count likelihoods and
  run-on tails.
type: software
authors:
